              another member, the _c_o_u_n_t parameter allows you to supply a posi‐
              tive  whole  number that selects the instance of the given name,
              with "1" indicating the first instance. If _N  is  not  specified
              the  first member of that name will be selected. If _c_o_u_n_t is not
              supplied, the operation fails.*count* cannot be

       oo      When extracting files, use the modification times of  any  _f_i_l_e_s
              as  they  appear in the aarrcchhiivvee. By default _f_i_l_e_s extracted from
              the archive use the time of extraction.

       OO      Display member offsets inside the archive.

       TT      Alias for ----tthhiinn. In many ar implementations TT has  a  different
              meaning, as specified by X/Open System interface.

       vv      When printing _f_i_l_e_s or the aarrcchhiivvee table of contents, this modi‐
              fier instructs llllvvmm--aarr to include additional information in  the
              output.

   MMooddiiffiieerrss ((ggeenneerriicc))
       The modifiers below may be applied to any operation.

       cc      For the _r (replace)and _q (quick update) operations, llllvvmm--aarr will
              always create  the  archive  if  it  doesn't  exist.   Normally,
              llllvvmm--aarr will print a warning message indicating that the aarrcchhiivvee
              is being created. Using this modifier turns off that warning.

       DD      Use zero for timestamps and UIDs/GIDs. This is set by default.

       PP      Use full paths when matching member names rather than  just  the
              file name.  This can be useful when manipulating an aarrcchhiivvee gen‐
              erated by another archiver, as some allow paths as member names.
              This is the default behavior for thin archives.

       ss      This  modifier  requests that an archive index (or symbol table)
              be added to the aarrcchhiivvee, as if using ranlib.  The  symbol  table
              will  contain  all  the  externally visible functions and global
              variables defined by all the bitcode files in  the  archive.  By
              default  llllvvmm--aarr  generates  symbol tables in archives. This can
              also be used as an operation.

       SS      This modifier is the opposite of the _s  modifier.  It  instructs
              llllvvmm--aarr to not build the symbol table. If both _s and _S are used,
              the last modifier to occur in the options will prevail.

       uu      Only update aarrcchhiivvee members with _f_i_l_e_s  that  have  more  recent
              timestamps.

       UU      Use actual timestamps and UIDs/GIDs.

